  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-07-06T16:40:23.273Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I believe there should be a performance tab in game that can do a few things. Below are some of the options.\n\n- Disable Dynamic Bones, This would allow a user to cause dynamic bone components on an avatar in the world to be disabled to increase performance of all avatars.\n\n- Disable Shadows, This option would either force all light sources in a world to No Shadow in the component or set all mesh/skinned mesh components to [Receive shadows, Cast shadows] disable.\n\n- Disable Particles, While there is now a way to set up a particle limiter it might be nice while in certain world or situations to completely disable them no matter what. Both world and avatar.\n\n- Render Distance, if there was a way to switch between different cameras with lower clipping planes, or even have avatars stop rendering all but name tags at a certain disable. Perhaps disable the skin/mesh renderers on all meshes in the avatar at a certain distance?\n\n- Auto Block, Similar to Block Avatars by Default however instead it blocks avatars with a poly count of above 60k total of all meshes including disabled ones like guns/weapons/etc. Or at least disables the visible ones if possible. The VRCSDK is able to check for poly count on enabled gameobjects so this should be do able in game.\n\n- Low Bandwidth Mode, This would prevent avatars that are above lets say 50mb from being downloaded and just disables a certain color of the blocked by default avatar. To show why that certain avatar is blocked.",
